{"id":"n5-049","title":"Verb て ください","romaji":"Verb-te kudasai","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"A request or command; 'please do'.","longExplanation":"The て ください grammar point is used to make a request or command someone to do something politely. The verb is conjugated into its て-form and followed by ください, which means 'please'. This structure is used when asking someone to do something with a polite and respectful tone.","formation":"Verb-て form + ください","examples":[{"jp":"ドアを開けてください。","romaji":"Doa wo akete kudasai.","en":"Please open the door.","words":[{"surface":"ドア","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"開け","vocabId":"1202450","reading":"あける","baseForm":"開ける"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184280","reading":"くださる","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"電話番号を教えてください。","romaji":"Denwa bangou wo oshiete kudasai.","en":"Please tell me your phone number.","words":[{"surface":"電話番号","vocabId":"1443940","reading":"でんわばんごう"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"教え","vocabId":"1236890","reading":"おしえ","baseForm":"教える"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184280","reading":"くださる","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"ゆっくり話してください。","romaji":"Yukkuri hanashite kudasai.","en":"Please speak slowly.","words":[{"surface":"ゆっくり","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話し","vocabId":"1562350","reading":"はなす","baseForm":"話す"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184280","reading":"くださる","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3]},{"jp":"コーヒーを一つ持ってきてください。","romaji":"Koohii wo hitotsu motte kite kudasai.","en":"Please bring me a coffee.","words":[{"surface":"コーヒー","vocabId":"1049180","reading":"コーヒー"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"一つ","vocabId":"1160820","reading":"ひとつ"},{"surface":"持っ","vocabId":"1315720","reading":"もつ","baseForm":"持つ"},{"surface":"て",